  "ref": "LEV.5.17",
  "review_notes": [
    "Two conditional conjunctions (אִם, כִּי) stand against one written *if*: אִם, at the clause head where the English word stands, takes it and כִּי is unrepresented under rule 22.",
    "מִצְוֺת is given the whole recasting *the things ... hath commanded*; the alternative confines it to *the things* and marks *hath commanded* added, which rule 20's supplied-lexical-verb clause would then have to license — rejected because the noun's own lexeme is what the English verb states."
  ]
